        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 2,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "In the evolving world of mobile application development, the rise of Progressive Web Applications (PWAs) has paved the way for new cross-platform runtimes. These runtimes enable web-based applications to be present in app stores without relying solely on native code. One such technology that facilitates this is "
        },
        {
          "type": "link",
          "location": {
            "line": 2,
            "column": 314
          },
          "url": "https://capacitorjs.com/",
          "title": null,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "location": {
                "line": 2,
                "column": 315
              },
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "location": {
                    "line": 2,
                    "column": 317
                  },
                  "text": "CapacitorJS"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 2,
            "column": 357
          },
          "text": ", which allows developers to deploy a simple website as an application across Android, iOS, and the web using a single JavaScript codebase. This approach significantly reduces development costs and increases coding efficiency."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 4,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 4,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "This guide will focus on creating an application using pure JavaScript without any additional frameworks. Despite the challenges of finding resources for pure JavaScript app development in 2021, we're here to provide you with a comprehensive tutorial on building your application and utilizing native plugins with CapacitorJS."
        }
      ]
    },
