          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 152,
            "column": 4
          },
          "text": "‣ Conclusion"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 154,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 154,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Developing cross-platform applications with CapacitorJS using pure JavaScript is a cost-effective and efficient way to create apps for multiple platforms with a single codebase. By following this guide, you've set up your project, restructured it for Vite, and prepared your app for development. With this foundation, you're well on your way to building a robust and versatile application."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "location": {
        "line": 156,
        "column": 1
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "location": {
            "line": 156,
            "column": 1
          },
          "text": "Remember to test thoroughly on all platforms and make use of Capacitor's native plugins to enhance your app's functionality. Happy coding!"
        }
      ]
    },
